.TH MREMAP 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
mremap \- resize or move a memory mapping
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/mman.h>
.B void* mremap(void* address, size_t old_size, size_t new_size,
.B              int flags, void* new_address);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resizes or moves a Linux mapping. All five arguments are required.
Pass zero as new_address unless MREMAP_FIXED is specified; that flag also
requires MREMAP_MAYMOVE. Use map_failed to check the result.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the new address, or the Linux MAP_FAILED sentinel (a pointer value
of \-1) with errno set. The header does not define a MAP_FAILED macro; use
map_failed to test the result.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR map_failed (3crunch),
.BR mmap (3crunch),
.BR mremap (2)
